nd\n   ```\n   #: The list of secret keys to try for verifying signatures, from\n        #: oldest to newest. The newest (last) key is used for signing.\n   ```\n\n2. `secret_key` property:\n   ```\n   return self.secret_keys[-1]\n   ```\n   with docstring \"The newest (last) entry in the :attr:`secret_keys` list.\"\n\n3. `derive_key`:\n   ```\n   if secret_key is None:\n            secret_key = self.secret_keys[-1]\n   ```\n\n4. `verify_signature`:\n   ```\n   for secret_key in reversed(self.secret_keys):\n   ```\n\n5. Serializer `iter_unsigners`:\n   ```\n   yield self.make_signer(salt)\n\n        for fallback in self.fallback_signers:\n            ...\n            for secret_key in self.secret_keys:\n                yield fallback(secret_key, salt=salt, **kwargs)\n   ```\n\n6. Serializer `loads`:\n   ```\n   for signer in self.iter_unsigners(salt):\n            try:\n                return self.load_payload(signer.unsign(s))\n   ```\n\n7. `_make_keys_list` helper:\n   ```\n   return [want_bytes(s) for s in secret_key]\n   ```\n\nI have all quotes from tool results already. Let me be careful with exact indentation. From the tool output:\n\nsigner.py `__init__`:\n```\n        #: The list of secret keys to try for verifying signatures, from\n        #: oldest to newest. The newest (last) key is used for signing.\n        #:\n        #: This allows a key rotation system to keep a list of allowed\n        #: keys and remove expired ones.\n        self.secret_keys: list[bytes] = _make_keys_list(secret_key)\n```\n\nsigner.py `secret_key` property:\n```\n    @property\n    def secret_key(self) -> bytes:\n        \"\"\"The newest (last) entry in the :attr:`secret_keys` list. This\n        is for compatibility from before key rotation support was added.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self.secret_keys[-1]\n```\n\nsigner.py `derive_key`:\n```\n        if secret_key is None:\n            secret_key = self.secret_keys[-1]\n```\n\nsigner.py `verify_signature`:\n```\n        fo